        // Sign-off needs a second pair of eyes: not the one who last finished the job.
        if (to === "signed") {
            const lastDone = job.history.find((m) => m.to === "done");
            if (lastDone !== undefined && lastDone.by === by) {
                return false;
            }
        }
>>>>>>> REPLACE
```

I changed the sign-off check so a move to `signed` is refused only when `by` exactly equals the `by` of the newest `done` move (found with `find`, since history is newest first). I couldn't see the rest of the file, so I'm relying on the comment that history is kept newest first; if it isn't, `find` would pick the wrong entry.
